    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having a nightmare with our jenkins pipeline. the unit test stage is being super flaky. it fails about 20% of the time but the codebase hasn't changed and the tests pass if i just retry the build. i've checked the basic stuff but i can't figure out what's causing these non-deterministic failures. any ideas on how to isolate the environment or what might be causing this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flaky unit tests are notorious for causing headaches in CI/CD pipelines. First, ensure your tests are truly isolated, meaning they don't rely on shared mutable state or external services that might be temporarily unavailable. Secondly, try running the test suite multiple times sequentially within the Jenkins agent to see if the failure pattern persists on repeated runs within the same environment. If it's still flaky, consider adding environment-specific logging or capturing state dumps immediately upon failure for better diagnostics.",
